ery racially diverse  community and so from the age of four or  five I'm in school and I'm in school  with kids of all different races and  it just never never occurred to me to  see it as anything strange or weird I  mean obviously I noticed that people  look differently from me but it would  never have even occurred to me to be  racist or to think that they're inferior  because they look different or because  they have a different color skin that  just just you know you don't think of it  most kids in a modern kindergarten or  first grade class you know they're  they're they're friends with all  different kids different races and it's  fine there's no problem it's only  society has to come in and complicate it  and start dividing which our society  actually does do that now it's it's not  socially acceptable anymore to come out  and to you know tell kids that certain  races are inferior so you don't have  that anymore but you do have race  baiters and race hustlers  in the media and in academia and all  over the place who are trying to defy  divide and make different races  suspicious of one another and so this  kind of discord and contempt and  suspicion and everything else which is a  damn shame because if you just let it  alone and let people live there wouldn't  be an issue I think about that famous  clip from Morgan Freeman where he was  asked on I think was 20 20 you know  years ago and he said what do we do  about race and how do we solve for a  sysm and his answer was stop talking  about it  just just shut up about it and and and  let people live and it'll be fine now  that wasn't always the solution but  nowadays it could be all right let's  leave it there all right hope you guys  have a great weekend find a way to get  out of the house at least if you can do  so without getting arrested and I'll  talk to you next week  Godspeed  the Matt Walsh show is produced by Sean  Hampton executive producer Jeremy boring  our supervising producers are Mathis  Glover